  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutionalizing Peace in Yemen- support to Track II mediation efforts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 18-month measure will identify suitable options for the establishment of a peace infrastructure in Yemen, and develop a roadmap for its functioning in any future transitional process. Any eventual peace infrastructure would explore the establishment of formal and informal structures devoted to peace and conflict management, as well as formulate clear policies for coordinating and supporting locally-led initiatives to prevent or resolve conflict. This measure will also include further support to the Mediation Support Fund, established under previous funding, which will continue to support locally-led mediation in governorates around Yemen. The primary beneficiary of this fund will continue to be the participants of the Youth Mediation Support Team programme that will receive specially-tailored training on peacebuilding and mediation-related topics. This programme has, throughout 2020 and 2021, proved to be an effective model for inclusive peacebuilding and for bridging between various tracks of the peacebuilding efforts.&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
